implementationPlan.description:
Overlay and final assembly in scripts/local-runner/source-export.mjs, plus test rows E5, E6 and E8.

Dirty paths:
- They are the union, deduplicated, of `diff --name-only -z --no-renames --no-ext-diff <commit> --` and `ls-files -z --others --exclude-standard`. Both run in the same envelope under the same deadline.
- Each path goes through validateImportPath first. A SNAPSHOT_CONTROL_PATH increments excluded and drops the path; any other path error propagates. So no filesystem call ever sees an unvalidated path.

Worktree read, for each kept path joined from the real root with path.join(root, ...segments):
- Every ancestor directory is lstat-ed, with the results cached per run. A symlink ancestor is snapshotError('SNAPSHOT_SYMLINK_DENIED'). A missing ancestor, or one that is not a directory, makes the path a delete.
- The path itself is lstat-ed:
  - ENOENT or ENOTDIR gives {kind:'delete', path};
  - a symlink is SNAPSHOT_SYMLINK_DENIED;
  - a directory (an untracked nested repository or a submodule worktree), or any other non-regular file, is EXPORT_ENTRY_UNSUPPORTED.
- A regular file:
  - open it with O_RDONLY | (O_NOFOLLOW ?? 0) | (O_NONBLOCK ?? 0); fstat must show a regular file with the lstat's dev and ino;
  - read at most size+1 bytes, so a file that grew past its fstat size is caught;
  - a read error is EXPORT_READ_FAILED, and the handle closes on every path.
- The running entry count and total of overlay file bytes are checked against MAX_IMPORT_ENTRIES and MAX_IMPORT_BYTES before each read (SNAPSHOT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED).
- executable: on POSIX, (stat.mode & 0o100) !== 0. On win32, it is the base listing's mode for a tracked path, and false for an untracked one.

Assembly: overlay = validateImport(overlayEntries). Resolve Object.freeze({ version: 1, commit, tree, base, overlay, excluded }).

Header comment additions:
- why both listings are used: a path removed from the index but still on disk appears in both;
- the v1 limits: a directory replaced by a file yields an ancestor collision that validateImport refuses; a line-ending-only difference is not dirty per git diff, so the base bytes stand;
- that nothing is ever written.

Tests, in the CQ-R09b section:
- E5 overlay. After the base commit:
  - modify one file, add an untracked nested file, delete one file, add a file that .gitignore ignores, and stage a new file;
  - the overlay holds exactly the modified, untracked, staged and deleted entries, each with the sha256 of its worktree bytes, and the ignored file is absent;
  - a dirty .moe/state.json is excluded and counted;
  - on POSIX, chmod +x shows executable true;
  - the dirt leaves base unchanged.
- E6, POSIX only (skip on win32 with a reason):
  - an untracked symlink, a tracked file replaced by a symlink, and a tracked directory replaced by a symlink to a directory holding a same-named file each refuse with SNAPSHOT_SYMLINK_DENIED;
  - the target's bytes are never read: put a FIFO or an unreadable file behind the link to prove it;
  - an untracked FIFO refuses with EXPORT_ENTRY_UNSUPPORTED.
- E8 read-only:
  - exporting a dirty repo leaves .git/index, .git/config, .git/HEAD, packed-refs and the loose refs byte-identical (hash them before and after);
  - on POSIX, a configured core.fsmonitor hook that would write a marker file never runs.

Error handling: every handle closes on every path, and a failure part-way leaves no partial snapshot.
